@startuml
title Who guarantees what - the trust chain behind a user-supplied proof

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #4A78B5
  LifeLineBorderColor #4A78B5
  ArrowColor #4A78B5
}
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #F7FAFF
skinparam noteBorderColor #4A78B5

participant "Compliance\noperator" as OP
participant "Denylist\nmint validator" as MINT
participant "Transaction\nbuilder" as TB
participant "Ledger\n(phase 1)" as LEDGER
participant "transfer_logic\nvalidator" as SCRIPT

== Once, when a sanction is added ==
OP -> MINT: AddToDenylist { user_pkh }
MINT -> MINT: is_admin power user + signature\nkey length == 28\nexactly one input bears the policy
MINT -> MINT: insert_ascending: spend the anchor,\nrewrite its link, emit the new node
note over MINT
  This is what makes a link
  TRUSTWORTHY later: no node's
  link can skip over a member.
  The expensive invariant is
  paid once, here.
end note

== Every transfer afterwards ==
TB -> TB: search the list off-chain,\nfind the covering node
TB -> LEDGER: transaction + reference input index
LEDGER -> LEDGER: resolve reference inputs\nagainst the live UTxO set
note right of LEDGER
  The builder supplies an INDEX.
  The ledger supplies the CONTENTS.
  A non-existent or spent UTxO is
  rejected before any script runs.
end note
LEDGER -> SCRIPT: Transaction (inputs, outputs,\nreference_inputs, redeemer)

SCRIPT -> SCRIPT: authenticate: one list NFT,\nwell-formed datum, key from asset name,\nstill at the denylist spend address
SCRIPT -> SCRIPT: covers_key: key < target < link,\nboth strict

alt both hold
  SCRIPT --> LEDGER: True - absence proved
else anything fails
  SCRIPT --> LEDGER: False or trap
  note right of SCRIPT
    Phase-2 validation is
    all-or-nothing, so the
    whole transaction fails.
  end note
end
@enduml
